eer bowed to me! I bowed back. Was that rude?","They really do bow before they take a cracker. But they also nibble maps."));Pt("nara_student",Lt("Our class trip is here tomorrow. Shikamori was the capital over twelve hundred years ago.","Before Tsukimiyako! Not many people remember that."));Pt("sign_nara_station",Lt(["鹿森駅 — Shikamori Station. Naramachi lanes are south, and Shikamori Park is further south past the shopping row.",""]));Pt("sign_naramachi",Lt("Naramachi — old merchant houses, now small shops and cafés. Please be quiet; people live here."));Pt("sign_nara_park",Lt("Shikamori Park. The deer here are wild animals, considered sacred messengers of the gods. Be gentle, and do not tease them."));Pt("nara_deer",Lt("The deer looks at you, then bows its head a little. It really wants a cracker.","Shika senbei are sold only at the stalls. Please do not feed them anything else."));Pt("nara_deer2",Lt("A sleepy deer lies in the sun and does not move for anyone.","Deer in Shikamori are protected as a national natural treasure."));Pt("nara_seller",Lt("Shika senbei! Two hundred yen a bundle.","Hold one up and they bow. Hold two up and they get excited. Hold none, and the deer will still check your pockets."));Pt("nara_kid",Lt("Look, look! I got three to bow at once!","そうだ！ I will feed the little one first!"));Pt("nara_priest",Lt("Welcome to the park of the Kasuga deer.","In old stories the god arrived at Shikamori riding on a white deer."));Pt("nara_grandma",Lt("I walk here every morning. The deer know my face by now.","Please keep your cracker bags closed until you are ready, dear."));Pt("nara_jogger",Lt("The park paths are flat and the air is lovely at dawn.","Just watch where you put your feet."));Pt("nara_craft",Lt("We make brushes and ink from old Shikamori recipes — it is one of the oldest crafts here."));Pt("nara_guide",Lt("Welcome to Daibutsu-ji. The Great Buddha is almost fifteen metres tall.","Its hall is one of the biggest wooden buildings in the world, though the one standing now is smaller than the first."));Pt("todaiji_deer",Lt("Even in the temple grounds the deer wander freely. They ignore the signs."));Pt("todaiji_monk",Lt("One pillar in the hall has a hole the size of the Buddha's nostril. Children crawl through it for luck.","Take your time; there is a line, but it moves."));Pt("sign_todaiji",Lt("大仏寺 — Daibutsu-ji. The Great Buddha Hall (大仏殿) stands behind this gate. Please keep quiet inside."));Pt("hiroshima_staff",[Ki("Welcome to Momijigawa.","ようこそ、紅葉川へ。"),Ki("Shinkansen to Hoshigaoka, Minatomachi and Tsurumi leave from this hall.")]);Pt("hiroshima_map",Lt("Area map: Momijigawa Station north, the main shopping streets and okonomiyaki lane in the middle, then the river and Crane Park to the south."));Pt("hiroshima_tourist",Lt("I came for the Crane Park and stayed for the okonomiyaki. The trams here are older than my grandmother.","Riding one is a treat."));Pt("hiroshima_student",Lt("We study about the city's history at school. It makes the peace message feel close."));Pt("sign_hiroshima_station",Lt(["紅葉川駅 — Momijigawa Station. The shopping streets are south; Crane Park is beyond the river.",""]));Pt("sign_peace",Lt("折り鶴公園 — Crane Park. A place to remember those who were lost and to wish for a world without war. Please be quiet and respectful."));Pt("hiroshima_guide",Lt("Welcome. Many people come to this park to think and to pray quietly.","People from all over the world fold paper cranes and send them here as wishes for peace."));Pt("hiroshima_kids",Lt("We folded one thousand paper cranes for our school! My crane is the yellow one.",'折り鶴 — orizuru — means "folded crane". People say a thousand cranes grant a wish.'));Pt("hiroshima_cook",Lt("Okonomiyaki: cabbage first, then pork, then the crepe. Momijigawa-style is a tower, not a mix.","Flip it only once. Show off with the spatula — that is the tradition."));Pt("hiroshima_tram",Lt("The tram goes slowly, so you can see the city. And it never runs out of seats at t